    <h2>How Refine Report Works</h2>
    <p>Refine Report is built into the main canvas of SARVARC Workspace, so it works with content you already have inside the platform rather than requiring a separate export and upload step.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Bring your content into the canvas.</strong> This can be data pulled from Data Arrangement, pages from the PDF Editor, or content collected through a published form.</li>
      <li><strong>Trigger Refine Report.</strong> One click applies your brand's color palette, logo, and typography across the document.</li>
      <li><strong>The layout is generated automatically.</strong> Section headings, spacing, header, and footer are structured consistently from the first page to the last.</li>
      <li><strong>Review and export.</strong> The finished report is ready to send as is, or you can make small adjustments directly in the canvas before exporting.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>There is no separate design step, no template to hunt down, and no back-and-forth between a document editor and a design tool just to get the branding right.</p>

    <div class="post-illustration-wrap">
      <img class="post-illustration" src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="Illustration of raw content flowing into a branded, ready-to-send report">
    </div>
    <p class="post-image-caption">From raw content to a branded, client-ready report in a single step</p>

    <div class="section-divider"><span class="diamond"></span></div>
    <h2>Where the Content in Your Report Comes From</h2>
    <p>Refine Report is only as useful as what feeds into it, and that is where the rest of SARVARC Workspace comes in. Data cleaned and structured in Data Arrangement can be pushed straight into a report section. Responses collected through <a href="https://sarvarc.com/blogs/sarvarc-forms/">SARVARC Forms</a> land as structured data that can flow directly into the same report without a manual export. Charts and diagrams built inside Workspace can be dropped into the layout the same way.</p>
    <p>This matters because a report is rarely written from scratch inside a blank document. It is usually assembled from data you already have somewhere else. Refine Report is designed to sit at the end of that pipeline, not as a separate tool you have to feed manually.</p>

    <div class="section-divider"><span class="diamond"></span></div>
    <h2>Client-Ready Means More Than Just Looking Good</h2>
    <p>A report that is genuinely client-ready needs to do three things at once: present information clearly, carry consistent branding, and be free of the small formatting errors that undermine credibility. Refine Report addresses all three by generating the layout from a fixed, brand-aware template logic rather than leaving formatting decisions to whoever is building the document that day.</p>
    <p>This also solves a quieter problem inside growing teams: formatting consistency across different people. When more than one person sends reports to clients, style drift is almost inevitable without a shared system. Refine Report enforces the same branded layout regardless of who generates the report, so every client-facing document looks like it came from the same company, because it did.</p>

    <div class="section-divider"><span class="diamond"></span></div>
    <h2>Refine Report Versus Manual Formatting Tools</h2>
    <p>Most businesses currently solve this problem with a mix of Word templates, Canva designs, or a designer's help for anything that needs to look polished. Each of these approaches works, but each one also adds a step: opening a separate tool, manually placing a logo, adjusting a template that was built for a different type of content, or waiting on someone else's availability.</p>
    <p>Refine Report removes that separate step by generating the branded layout directly from the content already inside your workspace. There is no template to keep updated by hand and no design software to open. The branding logic is applied automatically, every time, based on your actual brand assets.</p>

